3030214:00206530832:1866071101:0494/5029,4876,1039,120/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Bark Persia (of Boston), Holm, Cronstadt May 25, via Elsinore\nJune 2, with mdse. and pass. to Wm. Ropes & Co.", "lineage_id": "tribune:L58fec12b43dbdb7f", "source": "tribune", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030214/1866-07-11/ed-1/seq-8/"}, {"mark": "‖", "claim": "Passed Elsinore (1866-06-02)", "citation": "New York Herald, 23 June 1866, p. 3, col. 1", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_houseleek_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743555:1866062301:0195/39,1476,964,120/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "ELSINORE, June 2—Passed, bark Persia, Holm, from Cron-\nstadt for NYork.", "lineage_id": "herald:L84eaec03d9aa4ec2", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-06-23/ed-1/seq-3/"}, {"mark": "¶", "claim": "Brought news from Europe, to 1866-05-20", "citation": "New York Herald, 30 May 1866, p. 4, col. 1", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-30/ed-1/seq-4/", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_goldenglow_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743543:1866053001:1370/277,2308,968,164/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "By the arrival yesterday of the steamships St. David\noff Father Point and Persia at this port we have news\nfrom Europe to the 20th of May, three days later.", "lineage_id": "herald:L95254b5aa08409be", "source": "herald"}, {"mark": "7", "claim": "Brought news from Liverpool, to 1866-05-20", "citation": "New York Herald, 30 May 1866, p. 8, col. 1", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-30/ed-1/seq-8/", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": null, "verbatim": "The Cunard steamship Persia, Captain Lott, which left\nLiverpool at eleven o'clock on the morning of the 19th\nand Queenstown on the evening of the 20th of May,\narrived at this port yesterday evening.", "lineage_id": "herald:Lfcfc4c69726815be", "source": "herald"}, {"mark": "8", "claim": "Brought news from Liverpool, to 1866-06-30", "citation": "Evening Star (Washington), 12 July 1866, p. 2, col. 5", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83045462/1866-07-12/ed-1/seq-2/", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_leonberger_ver03:data:sn83045462:00280654279:1866071201:0093/3963,2308,1040,226/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "SANDY HOOK, July 12, 8.10 a. m.[?]—The steam-\ner Persia, from Liverpool on the 30th ult., via\nQueenstown on July 1st, has passed this\npoint.", "lineage_id": "star:L3fdb781543d1721e", "source": "star"}], "aboard": {"specie": [], "passengers": [{"n": 2, "marks": ["†"]}], "mails": [], "headlines": [{"text": "THE WAR IN EUROPE. Important News.", "dates_to": "1866-06-30", "marks": ["8"]}], "mail": []}}